! The displaced silicon of si2-nc-force.in on a *shifted* grid, with no symmetry.
!
! This case exists to separate two things that a shifted Monkhorst-Pack grid
! mixes together, because the difference between them is 1e-4 Ry and it took a
! relaxation to notice.
!
! A shifted grid is **not invariant under every symmetry operation the crystal
! has**. For this displaced cell, 4 of the 8 operations map the 4x4x4 shifted
! grid onto itself and 4 do not. A density built from that k-sample therefore
! does not have the four symmetries the crystal does -- and both this code and
! Quantum ESPRESSO symmetrise it with a set of operations that includes some it
! does not have. They pick *different* sets (see PLAN.md, P6), so their totals
! differ by ~1e-4 Ry, which is a hundred thousand times the agreement everything
! else in this suite reaches.
!
! With `nosym` there is nothing to disagree about: the same 64 k-points, no
! symmetrisation, and the two codes agree to the last digit either prints. That
! is what this case pins. It is the evidence that the SCF, the basis and the
! k-point generation are identical and that the spread above is a choice about
! symmetry rather than an error in the physics.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=12.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.27 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 1 1 1
